---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { writingPostBySlug } from '../../data/writing';

const post = writingPostBySlug['crypto-native'];

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: post.title,
  description: post.subtitle,
  image: `https://juanesquivel.xyz${post.cover}`,
  datePublished: post.publishedTime,
  author: {
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: 'Juan Esquivel',
    url: 'https://juanesquivel.xyz',
  },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'Juan Esquivel',
    url: 'https://juanesquivel.xyz',
    logo: {
      '@type': 'ImageObject',
      url: 'https://juanesquivel.xyz/images/avatar.jpg',
    },
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': 'https://juanesquivel.xyz/writing/crypto-native',
  },
};
---

<Layout
  title="Why Crypto-Native Still Matters — Juan Esquivel"
  description="Why being crypto-native still matters as the industry matures. Lessons on building intuition for what's real in web3, drawn from experience inside the space."
  type="article"
  image={post.cover}
  publishedTime={post.publishedTime}
  canonicalPath="/writing/crypto-native"
  preloadImages={[post.cover]}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <nav class="nav">
    <a href="/writing" class="back-link">
      <svg
        width="16"
        height="16"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
      >
        <path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path>
      </svg>
      Writing
    </a>
  </nav>

  <article class="post">
    {
      post.cover && (
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img
            src={post.cover}
            alt="Crypto-native article cover"
            width="640"
            height="360"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </figure>
      )
    }

    <header class="post-header">
      <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
      <p class="post-subtitle">{post.subtitle}</p>
      <div class="post-meta">
        <time>{post.date}</time>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="post-content">
      <p>
        Been in this space since 2021. Being crypto-native isn't the flex it used to be. But it's
        still an advantage.
      </p>

      <h2>For the Individual</h2>

      <p>
        It helps you distinguish vaporware from real products. Mostly. You've been around long
        enough to see what ships and what doesn't. This helps when you're looking to join a team,
        work with someone, or bet your time on something.
      </p>

      <p>
        It helps you distinguish hype cycles from real value. You've seen people and companies chase
        trends. You build an understanding of what is often just hype and what might be worth the
        effort.
      </p>

      <p>
        You know the players. Who's credible, who's actually built things. You can spot the other
        natives in the space vs the tourists.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you're still around after so much pain, you're a sadist or you just really believe in the
        technology and its potential.
      </p>

      <h2>For the Teams</h2>

      <p>
        They speak the language. If you're still ecosystem-facing (which most teams are even with
        increasing institutional adoption), natives understand the culture, what resonates and what
        falls flat.
      </p>

      <p>
        They come with network. They've built relationships with founders, contributors, operators.
        They've connected with people across CT, conferences, and Telegram group chats.
      </p>

      <p>
        They attract other natives. Crypto-native talent wants to work with people who get it.
        Hiring one makes it easier to hire the next.
      </p>

      <p>
        They're not here short-term. They already survived the cycles. They're not leaving when it
        gets hard.
      </p>

      <h2>The Trend is Real</h2>

      <p>
        Trad (web2) talent has been coming in for years. Across different cycles, in different
        waves, in different amounts. The roles are following the product adoption curve and who's
        buying. More product marketing, more enterprise sales, more fintech customers that didn't
        really exist five years ago.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our companies have matured. They'll naturally need functions crypto-natives never had to
        fill. Many incumbents sit at the intersection of ecosystem and institutions. They need both
        languages. This isn't a bad thing. It's a sign the industry is actually going somewhere.
      </p>

      <h2>The Point</h2>

      <p>
        Crypto-native doesn't mean you've got it all. It means you've built intuition for what's
        real in an industry that's filled with noise. That has to be worth something?
      </p>

      <p>
        But intuition alone isn't enough. The industry is going to keep changing. The natives who
        stay relevant aren't the ones who rest on "I was here early." They're the ones who keep
        learning.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="more-writing">
    <h2>More writing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/writing/building-way-in">A Story About Building Your Way In</a></li>
      <li>
        <a href="/writing/stablepod-lessons"
          >The best crypto founders and leaders do this on podcasts</a>
      </li>
      <li><a href="/writing">See all writing</a></li>
    </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .nav {
    margin-bottom: 2.35rem;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .back-link:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--line-strong);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .post {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .post-cover,
  .post-image {
    margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
  }

  .post-cover img,
  .post-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .post-image figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .post-header {
    margin-bottom: 2.35rem;
  }

  .post-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98; margin-bottom: 0.95rem;
  }

  .post-subtitle {
    max-width: 40ch; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-soft); line-height: 1.78; margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .post-meta {
    color: var(--text-faint);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .post-content {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .post-content h2 {
    margin-top: 2.6rem; margin-bottom: 1.05rem; font-size: 1.52rem;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .post-content h3 {
    margin-top: 1.9rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem; font-size: 1.16rem;
    text-transform: none;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .post-content p,
  .post-content li {
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.84;
  }

  .post-content p + p,
  .post-content p + ul,
  .post-content p + blockquote,
  .post-content p + .post-image,
  .post-content ul + p,
  .post-content blockquote + p,
  .post-content .post-image + p,
  .post-content h2 + p,
  .post-content h3 + p {
    margin-top: 1.08rem;
  }

  .post-content ul {
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .post-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.45rem;
  }

  .post-content blockquote {
    margin-top: 1.08rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    color: var(--text);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .post-content hr {
    border: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .post-content strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .post-content em {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  .post-content code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875em;
    background: var(--surface-strong);
    padding: 0.18em 0.38em;
  }

  .post-content pre {
    margin-top: 1.08rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
  }

  .post-content pre code {
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .post-content a,
  .more-writing a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--text-faint);
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .more-writing {
    margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .more-writing h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.95rem;
  }

  .more-writing ul {
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
</style>
